<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Morris (2012), Mooi & David (1998) & Meinhardt (2008) echinoderm bilateral-to-pentaradial hydrocoel ring symmetry breaking & Lovén's Law — MorphoEval overall 51.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py` (consensus score 52.7/100). Evaluates an algebraic dispersion curve on a static circle to pick m* = 5 (72 deg), but omits a genuine Gierer-Meinhardt reaction-diffusion PDE simulation on a closing hydrocoel crescent-to-ring domain, omits Lovén's Law (1874) asymmetric initiation sequence (II, IV, I, III, V) and biserial peristomial plate enlargement (ba-ab-ba-ab-ab), omits Duboc et al. (2005) right-sided Nodal knockdown twin-rudiment (2x5 = 10 podia) perturbation, lacks polar Fourier C_5 harmonic segmentation of the vendored Tripneustes gratilla echinoid test specimen, and lacks runtime SHA-256 dataset verification. Overall 51.7/100 (faithfulness 49.6, reproducibility 56.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit HEAD; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 54, Morphological realism / specimen match 46, Parameter expressivity 49, Morphometric validation 50, Source and data traceability 62, Code-to-model traceability 55, Reproducibility package 53. Output judged: docs/media/echinoderm_pentaradial_symmetry_comparison.png: rendered output of 2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py at HEAD, image/png, 659701 B, 1331×1177 px, artifact_sha256 28b98789b0b6280378531cfa4ba7608dd7f541e0956961716449cc8b8db7022f (sha256 28b98789b0b6280378531cfa4ba7608dd7f541e0956961716449cc8b8db7022f), spec_fingerprint f94f62955d7ff6974c8a237ced577144db975e6e7e74430aca24de11b763608f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: f94f62955d7ff6974c8a237ced577144db975e6e7e74430aca24de11b763608f; artifact_sha256: 28b98789b0b6280378531cfa4ba7608dd7f541e0956961716449cc8b8db7022f; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/echinoderm_pentaradial_symmetry/echinoderm_pentaradial_symmetry_reference.json=c516e298727883cf..., datasets/echinoderm_pentaradial_symmetry/echinoderm_pentaradial_test_specimen.jpg=953b2f7e38029627..., datasets/echinoderm_pentaradial_symmetry/scout_manifest.json=0b333ebe2a2ed524...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Implement Duboc et al. (2005) right-sided Nodal/BMP2-4 left-right symmetry breaking and its perturbations: wild-type single left rudiment (1x5 = 5 podia), Nodal morpholino knockdown bilateral twin rudiments (2x5 = 10 podia), and ectopic bilateral Nodal overexpression (0 podia).",
        "remediation needed: Implement a time-stepped Gierer-Meinhardt activator-inhibitor reaction-diffusion PDE on a closing hydrocoel crescent-to-ring domain, demonstrating spontaneous m^* = 5 (Delta_theta = 72 deg) lobe formation and sequential anterior-to-posterior initiation matching Lovén's Law (II, IV, I, III, V) and the asymmetric biserial peristomial plate law (Ib, IIb, IIIa, IVa, Va).",
        "remediation needed: Implement automated polar Fourier C_5 harmonic segmentation (`segment_echinoid_test_specimen`) on `echinoderm_pentaradial_test_specimen.jpg` to detect the 5 ambulacral rays (72.0 +/- 1.4 deg spacing, C_5 fundamental power fraction 0.9255), plus runtime SHA-256 dataset verification, 9 morphometrics in `measure_morphoeval()`, and an 8-check `self_test()` suite.",
        "remediation needed: Implement the full hydrocoel circumference-to-wavelength mode selection staircase m^* in {3, 4, 5, 6, 7} vs 2*pi*R_ring/lambda_c alongside a homogeneous sub-threshold negative control (D_h = D_a, zero spatial Turing instability)." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.17e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

